+# Connecting the account screen
+
+This repository contains a static site, with no authentication or server code. The account screen defaults to an explicitly labeled preview with three sample passkeys, persisted in localStorage. Preview mode never calls WebAuthn or changes real credentials.
+
+To use real customer data, implement the same-origin API below and add `data-account-mode="live"` to the `<html>` element. Serve the account route using this page (or integrate the screen into the authenticated account template). Never enable live mode without a backend that authenticates every request and scopes records to the current customer. No framework fallback to preview occurs on API errors.
+
+## API
+
+- `GET /api/account/passkeys`: return the complete list for the signed-in customer.
+- `PATCH /api/account/passkeys/:id`: accept `{ "name": "New name" }`; trim and validate names to 1–64 characters.
+- `DELETE /api/account/passkeys/:id`: revoke the credential on the server before responding. Enforce any last-passkey or recovery requirements server-side. Do not revoke the customer’s current session solely because its passkey was deleted.
+
+All three return the authoritative JSON snapshot below. Mutation responses must contain the complete updated list, including credential IDs; do not paginate it. Use an atomic transaction to mutate and read the resulting list. The GET endpoint and responses should use `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "authenticated": true,
+  "complete": true,
+  "rpId": "coffee.example.com",
+  "userId": "dXNlcjEyMw",
+  "csrfToken": "session-bound-csrf-token",
+  "passkeys": [
+    {
+      "id": "database-record-id",
+      "credentialId": "Y3JlZGVudGlhbDEyMw",
+      "name": "MacBook Pro",
+      "device": "laptop",
+      "createdAt": "2026-09-12T10:30:00Z",
+      "lastUsedAt": "2026-10-28T08:15:00Z",
+      "current": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+`userId` is the original WebAuthn user handle and `credentialId` is the raw credential ID, both encoded as unpadded base64url. `rpId` must be the registration RP ID. `current` means this credential authenticated the current session, not that the browser necessarily stores it. Device icons accept `laptop`, `phone`, or `key` (the default).
+
+Use secure, HttpOnly, SameSite session cookies. Mutations send the snapshot’s CSRF token through `X-CSRF-Token`; validate it, the request origin, session ownership, and record ownership server-side. Return 401/403 for unauthenticated/unauthorized requests and 409 for stale records. Every success response must reflect the committed mutation. The client must not be trusted for authorization.
+
+## Browser authenticator sync
+
+In live mode, after loading a validated complete snapshot and after confirmed deletion, the client feature-detects `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials` and sends the RP ID, user handle, and complete accepted credential list. Preview data is never signaled. A final deletion intentionally signals an empty list for that user. Do not pass filtered or paginated lists because omitted credentials may be removed from the authenticator.
+
+Unsupported browsers and failed signals show device-settings guidance without undoing a committed server deletion. Successful signaling means the browser was notified; the authenticator controls actual synchronization. Labels are account-only: WebAuthn has no signal for renaming individual credential labels. `signalCurrentUserDetails` changes the account user details and must not be used to rename a passkey.
+
+Reference: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api
